{"availability":"available","full":"imtiazither/eduwork-databridge","name":"eduwork-databridge","description":"Open-source reference framework for governed learning and workforce data interoperability, quality, identity review, lineage, and exports.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":17,"forks":5,"created":"2026-07-20T19:56:56Z","updated":"2026-10-04T05:01:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://imtiazither.github.io/eduwork-databridge/","topics":[],"demo":"https://imtiazither.github.io/eduwork-databridge/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:12:07.078Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:12:07.078Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:12:07.078Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:12:07.078Z","stars":17,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["v0.20.0 adds a protected match-review queue and workload summary. Authorized reviewers can list candidates, filter by current status, page through the queue, see the latest reasoned decision, and measure how many candidates remain unreviewed.","EduWork DataBridge is an open-source platform for making that reconciliation inspectable. It keeps source evidence, checks the awkward records, separates uncertain identity matches from safe ones, and carries lineage into governed outputs.","One training report may need an employee roster from HR, completion records from an LMS, scores from an assessment file, and awards from a credential system. The joins usually happen in a spreadsheet. When an ID is missing or two accounts look alike, the reasoning can disappear inside the finished report."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imtiazither/eduwork-databridge/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0e5c98da2958c9b57330c7a77958e275c55c4eed8dd0a89bc7598bb930c48757","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:37.756Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:12:37.756Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"v0.20.0 adds a protecte